  context.LocalComputed.TheseGlobalValues = "This global value"
  context.LocalComputed.Defaults = "the default"
  context.LocalComputed.Them = "it"
  context.LocalComputed.Parameters = "parameter"
  context.LocalComputed.Are = "is"
}

context.LocalComputed.May = "may"
if (context.Local.HasRequired) {
  context.LocalComputed.May = "must"
}
sjs```
{{- $op := .Local.Usage.Operation -}}

{{.LocalComputed.CertainParameters}} {{.LocalComputed.Are}} configured globally. {{.LocalComputed.TheseParameters}} {{.LocalComputed.May}} be set on the SDK client instance itself during initialization. When configured as an option during SDK initialization, {{.LocalComputed.TheseGlobalValues}} will be used as {{.LocalComputed.Defaults}} on the operations that use {{.LocalComputed.Them}}. When such operations are called, there is a place in each to override the global value, if needed.
{{with .Local.ExampleParameter}}
For example, you can set `{{.Name}}` to `{{templateReadmeGlobalValue .}}` at SDK initialization and then you do not have to pass the same value on calls to operations like `{{sanitizeMethodName $op}}`. But if you want to do so you may, which will locally override the global setting. See the example code below for a demonstration.
{{end}}

